 870:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Function description
 871:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Stores string in SEGGER RTT control block.
 872:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    This data is read by the host.
 873:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 874:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Parameters
 875:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    BufferIndex  Index of "Up"-buffer to be used (e.g. 0 for "Terminal").
 876:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    s            Pointer to string.
 877:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 878:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Return value
 879:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Number of bytes which have been stored in the "Up"-buffer.
 880:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 881:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Notes
 882:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (1) If there is not enough space in the "Up"-buffer, depending on configuration,
 883:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        remaining characters may be dropped or RTT module waits until there is more space in the b
 884:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (2) String passed to this function has to be \0 terminated
 885:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (3) \0 termination character is *not* stored in RTT buffer
 886:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** */
